{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>If the ox gore a slave.</b> In the case of a warned ox, for if it were an unwarned ox, the value of a slave would turn out to be greater than the value of a free person." "<b>Thirty shekels of silver.</b> Corresponding to the valuation of a female from twenty years old until sixty, for a slave and a woman are equivalent, since it derives this from a woman." "<b>And the ox shall be stoned.</b> Lest it kill a free person, since it has begun to gore. And because it is the habit of a slave to be found among the animals to guard them and to feed them, and sometimes they kill him, and the parties come to dispute, this one saying: my slave was worth such and such, and that one saying: he was worth only such and such — therefore it fixed a set amount for their death, thirty shekels. But a free person is an uncommon case."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:37.742449604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}